WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.930
To make lime, limestone is heated in
a kiln to about 900 degrees Celsius.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.030
Leave limestone at room temperature,
and it simply stays as limestone.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.930
The reaction is the same
at both temperatures.

4
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.470
So why does it need such a hot kiln?

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.450
Why does limestone need a kiln at
about 900 degrees to turn into lime?

6
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.890
In this mission, you'll find out why the
entropy of the surroundings counts too,

7
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.690
and combine everything into
one value: Gibbs energy.

8
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.750
You'll calculate ΔG at
different temperatures,

9
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.610
and see how it is built
from enthalpy and entropy.

10
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: explain why limestone
must be strongly heated to make lime.
